jobs_results.description:
COFCO International is a global agri-business with a clear vision, strong values and a positive culture, focused on being a leader in the global grains, oilseeds and sugar supply chains. We provide the food the world needs in a responsible way. Headquartered is Geneva, Switzerland, we are ambitious, with the right structures and culture to meet the world's increasing and changing needs. With 11,000+ people in 35 countries, our global portfolio includes assets across the Americas, Europe, Africa, Middle East, and Asia-Pacific. We trade with over 50 nations, while providing farmers unique direct access to the growing Chinese market.

Job Purpose

We offer an exciting role as SAP ABAP development within IT SAP Development Team of COFCO International. The position gives an opportunity to work in several projects and multi-country implementation in an international environment. The CIL SAP system covers finance, procurement, logistics, production, plant maintenance and trade integration... processes for 3,000 users. These systems are used worldwide in all of CIL’s offices.

Job Responsibilities

The ABAP/FIORI developer will be responsible for developments of ABAP and Fiori applications for both new projects and support activities. Usage of modern approaches, including RAP, Fiori Elements and SAP best practices – keeping focus on standard.

Process oriented developments and functional knowledge – capable of supporting unit tests and integrations are important.

Requirements
• Degree in Computer Science or equivalent;
• 2 to 4 years of experience in SAP ABAP;
• 2 years of experience in UI5/Fiori Development;
• Prior experience in ABAP O-O and SAP FIORI/U5 Development;
• Good knowledge of SAP modules such as FICO, MM;
• Must have the capability to work well in a team-based environment;
• Significant experience of working within a SAP system incorporating support and project management, including a number of implementations;
• Technical Experience in:
• CDS ABAP development;
• UI5 and Fiori Elements;
• Enhancement Framework (BADI’s, EP, User-Exits);
• Adobe Forms and Smartforms;
• Performance driven programming;
• Webservice integration;
• Error Tracking and Analysis;
• HANA Development (preferred);
• AIF (preferred).
• Drive and ability to take initiatives independently;
• International experience and experience working with global ERP roll-outs;
• Experience within Agri-Commodity trading Industry (plus);
• Fluent in Engish.

We kindly ask you to submit your CV in English.

COFCO International is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, age, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status or any other characteristic protected by law. www.cofcointernational.com

